// What burns and what it burns in. Temperatures in °F, as tuned in the old game (old FuelType).
// Loaded once by Content; ContentTests checks every name in here resolves.
//
// fuels: the resources that burn; a resource with no row here does not. peakTempF is how hot it can
//   make a fire; minFireTempF is how hot the fire must already be before it catches; ignitionBonusPct
//   is what it adds to the odds of starting a fire as tinder.
// pits: every PitType. maxFuelKg is what it holds; windProtectionLevel how much wind it keeps off the
//   flames; fuelEfficiencyFactor how much longer fuel lasts in it.
// deterrence: what flame does to an animal's nerve (Combat.FireDeterrence).
//   fireFear is the one base value for every animal (people are not deterred): what a flame at full
//   intensity, close by, takes off its resolve. torchIntensityPct is what a lit torch counts for against a
//   campfire's 1. fullIntensityHeatF is the radiant heat (Fire.HeatOutputF against 0 °F air) at which a pit
//   counts in full: a steady to roaring wood fire. fullWithinM is the distance inside which a flame
//   deters in full; beyond it, deterrence falls off with the square of the distance.
{
